IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `niis-dates`
IMPORT `niis-core`
IMPORT `niis-seat`

-- National Injury Insurance Scheme (Queensland) Act 2016 -- cases from the seat of the injured person.
--
-- Every expected value is worked by hand from the deposited text, with the arithmetic in the comment above it; none was
-- copied from the encoding's output. The regulative rules are run with EVALTRACE where the trace ends FULFILLED, and
-- #TRACEd with an "-- expect:" line where it ends in a breach. Clock: days.
--
-- Readings used (niis-dates.l4): "within 28 days after" a day ends 28 days later; "within 6 months" or "1 year after"
-- ends on the same day 6 months or a year later (or the last day of a shorter month); "at least 1 month before" a day
-- ends on the same day a month earlier; "at least 10 business days before" ends on the 10th business day counted back.
--
-- The story: Mia was a passenger in a car with CTP insurance that collided with a truck on the Bruce Highway near
-- Gympie on 14 March 2025. She suffered a permanent spinal cord injury. HYPOTHETICAL facts throughout; the regulation's
-- figures (eligibility criteria, buy-in, payment limits, waiting period) are not deposited and are given as facts.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

`d` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY

`spinal` MEANS `a permanent spinal cord injury resulting in a permanent neurological deficit`
`CTP car` MEANS `a motor vehicle with a CTP insurance policy in force`
`collision` MEANS `a collision, or action taken to avoid a collision, with the vehicle`
`no holidays` MEANS EMPTY

§ `s 4 -- does the Act apply`

-- Mia: every s 4(1) condition met, no s 4(2)-(3) exclusion.
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` `spinal` `CTP car` `collision` `an ordinary vehicle` `on a road` TRUE (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS `the Act applies to the injury`
-- The commencement edge: 1 July 2016 is in; 30 June 2016 is not (s 4(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` `spinal` `CTP car` `collision` `an ordinary vehicle` `on a road` TRUE (`d` 1 7 2016) FALSE EQUALS `the Act applies to the injury`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` `spinal` `CTP car` `collision` `an ordinary vehicle` `on a road` TRUE (`d` 30 6 2016) FALSE EQUALS `no: the motor accident did not happen in Queensland on or after 1 July 2016 (s 4(1)(b))`
-- An accident in New South Wales.
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` `spinal` `CTP car` `collision` `an ordinary vehicle` `on a road` FALSE (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS `no: the motor accident did not happen in Queensland on or after 1 July 2016 (s 4(1)(b))`
-- A broken leg is not in the schedule 1 list ("means").
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` `another personal injury` `CTP car` `collision` `an ordinary vehicle` `on a road` TRUE (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS `no: the injury is not a serious personal injury`
-- Each of the other serious personal injuries counts: amputation of a leg through the femur; blindness.
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` `the amputation of a leg through or above the femur` `CTP car` `collision` `an ordinary vehicle` `on a road` TRUE (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS `the Act applies to the injury`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` `permanent blindness caused by a trauma` `CTP car` `the driving of the vehicle` `an ordinary vehicle` `on a road` TRUE (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS `the Act applies to the injury`
-- No prescribed vehicle (s 7).
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` `spinal` `a vehicle that is none of these` `collision` `an ordinary vehicle` `on a road` TRUE (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS `no: no prescribed vehicle was involved (s 7)`
-- Injured some other way (for example, struck by a load falling from a parked truck being unloaded).
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` `spinal` `CTP car` `some other way` `an ordinary vehicle` `on a road` TRUE (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS `no: the injury did not result from the vehicle in a way s 4(1)(a) lists`
-- s 4(2): an uninsured car on private land: no. In a public place (a shopping centre car park): yes.
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` `spinal` `an uninsured motor vehicle to which a nominal defendant scheme applies` `the vehicle running out of control` `an ordinary vehicle` `somewhere else` TRUE (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS `no: an uninsured motor vehicle, and the accident was not on a road or in a public place (s 4(2))`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` `spinal` `an uninsured motor vehicle to which a nominal defendant scheme applies` `the vehicle running out of control` `an ordinary vehicle` `in a public place that is not a road` TRUE (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS `the Act applies to the injury`
-- s 4(4)(c): an uninsured trailer is not an "uninsured motor vehicle", so s 4(2) does not reach it.
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` `spinal` `an uninsured trailer to which a nominal defendant scheme applies` `collision` `an ordinary vehicle` `somewhere else` TRUE (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS `the Act applies to the injury`
-- Fork line 1: an unidentified vehicle on private land is not shown to be uninsured.
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` `spinal` `an unidentified motor vehicle or trailer to which a nominal defendant scheme applies` `collision` `an ordinary vehicle` `somewhere else` TRUE (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS `the Act applies to the injury`
-- s 4(3)(a): an insured tractor in a public place: no; on a road: yes. An uninsured forklift on a road: s 4(2) does not
-- apply to it ("other than a prescribed vehicle stated in subsection (3)(a)"), and it is on a road: yes.
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` `spinal` `CTP car` `the driving of the vehicle` `a tractor, backhoe, bulldozer, end-loader, forklift, industrial crane or hoist, or other mobile machinery` `in a public place that is not a road` TRUE (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS `no: a vehicle of a kind in s 4(3)(a), and the accident was not on a road`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` `spinal` `CTP car` `the driving of the vehicle` `a tractor, backhoe, bulldozer, end-loader, forklift, industrial crane or hoist, or other mobile machinery` `on a road` TRUE (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS `the Act applies to the injury`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` `spinal` `an uninsured motor vehicle to which a nominal defendant scheme applies` `the driving of the vehicle` `a tractor, backhoe, bulldozer, end-loader, forklift, industrial crane or hoist, or other mobile machinery` `on a road` TRUE (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS `the Act applies to the injury`
-- An agricultural machine on a farm: no.
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` `spinal` `CTP car` `the vehicle running out of control` `an agricultural machine being used for agricultural purposes` `somewhere else` TRUE (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS `no: a vehicle of a kind in s 4(3)(a), and the accident was not on a road`
-- s 4(3)(b): terrorism.
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` `spinal` `CTP car` `collision` `an ordinary vehicle` `on a road` TRUE (`d` 14 3 2025) TRUE EQUALS `no: the vehicle was being used for an act of terrorism (s 4(3)(b))`

§ `s 12 -- eligibility`

-- Mia meets the criteria, no damages yet, no earlier condition.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to participate in the scheme` `spinal` `CTP car` `collision` `an ordinary vehicle` `on a road` TRUE (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `eligible to participate in the scheme (s 12)`
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to participate in the scheme` `spinal` `CTP car` `collision` `an ordinary vehicle` `on a road` TRUE (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not eligible: the injury does not meet the eligibility criteria prescribed by regulation (s 12(1)(b))`
-- An accident in 2015: the Act does not apply.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to participate in the scheme` `spinal` `CTP car` `collision` `an ordinary vehicle` `on a road` TRUE (`d` 14 3 2015) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not eligible: the Act does not apply to the injury (s 12(1)(a))`
-- s 12(2): care damages awarded and paid by the insurer: not eligible. Paid by the agency under s 44(3)(a): eligible.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to participate in the scheme` `spinal` `CTP car` `collision` `an ordinary vehicle` `on a road` TRUE (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not eligible: damages for treatment, care and support needs were awarded and paid other than by the agency under s 44(3)(a) (s 12(2))`
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to participate in the scheme` `spinal` `CTP car` `collision` `an ordinary vehicle` `on a road` TRUE (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `eligible to participate in the scheme (s 12)`
-- s 12(3): an earlier condition the accident did not permanently worsen: not eligible; one it did: eligible.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to participate in the scheme` `spinal` `CTP car` `collision` `an ordinary vehicle` `on a road` TRUE (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not eligible: the injury did not permanently increase a disability the person already had (s 12(3))`
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to participate in the scheme` `spinal` `CTP car` `collision` `an ordinary vehicle` `on a road` TRUE (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `eligible to participate in the scheme (s 12)`

§ `s 13 -- buying in`

#ASSERT `Can I buy into the scheme` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `s 13 does not apply: the person is eligible under s 12, and applies under s 16`
#ASSERT `Can I buy into the scheme` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 13 does not apply: the injury is not one prescribed by regulation for buying in`
#ASSERT `Can I buy into the scheme` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the agency may accept the person as a buy-in participant for an agreed period; the contribution must then be paid within 28 days (s 13(2)-(4))`
-- s 13(4): accepted 10 February 2026; 28 days later (18 to 28 February, 10 into March) is 10 March 2026.
#ASSERT `Am I still a buy-in participant` (`d` 10 2 2026) TRUE (`d` 10 3 2026) (`d` 10 3 2026) EQUALS `a buy-in participant: the contribution was paid in time`
#ASSERT `Am I still a buy-in participant` (`d` 10 2 2026) FALSE (`a date not used`) (`d` 10 3 2026) EQUALS `a buy-in participant for now; the contribution must be paid by` (`d` 10 3 2026)
#ASSERT `Am I still a buy-in participant` (`d` 10 2 2026) FALSE (`a date not used`) (`d` 11 3 2026) EQUALS `no longer a participant, and taken never to have been one (s 13(4))`
-- Paid a day late: s 13(4) has already taken effect.
#ASSERT `Am I still a buy-in participant` (`d` 10 2 2026) TRUE (`d` 11 3 2026) (`d` 11 3 2026) EQUALS `no longer a participant, and taken never to have been one (s 13(4))`
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `s 13 -- the buy-in participant must pay the contribution within 28 days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the participant` `pay the buy-in contribution` 28)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the participant, "s 13(4): the contribution was not paid within 28 days ..." (paid on day 29)
#TRACE `s 13 -- the buy-in participant must pay the contribution within 28 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the participant` DOES `pay the buy-in contribution` AT 29

§ `ss 10, 16-18 -- applying`

-- s 16(2): Mia's accident on 14 March 2025: the application period ends on 14 March 2026. An accident on 29 February
-- 2024: 2025 has no 29 February, so 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT `By when should I apply` (`d` 14 3 2025) EQUALS `the application period ends on` (`d` 14 3 2026)
#ASSERT `By when should I apply` (`d` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `the application period ends on` (`d` 28 2 2025)
#ASSERT `Must the agency accept my application` (`d` 14 3 2025) (`d` 14 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `the agency must accept the application (s 16(2))`
#ASSERT `Must the agency accept my application` (`d` 14 3 2025) (`d` 15 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `the application is late: the agency decides whether it is fair and reasonable to accept it (s 16(3)-(4))`
#ASSERT `Must the agency accept my application` (`d` 14 3 2025) (`d` 1 4 2025) TRUE EQUALS `s 16(2) and (3) do not apply after a s 44(3)(a) payment (s 17(4)(b)); even if the injured person is eligible, the agency may refuse unless it is satisfied of severe financial hardship (s 22(4)-(5))`

-- s 17: nothing in the way.
#ASSERT `Can I apply now` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`a date not used`) 5 TRUE (`d` 1 4 2025) EQUALS `an application may be made`
#ASSERT `Can I apply now` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`a date not used`) 5 TRUE (`d` 1 4 2025) EQUALS `no: another application for the injury has not been decided (s 17(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can I apply now` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`a date not used`) 5 TRUE (`d` 1 4 2025) EQUALS `no: the injured person is already an interim participant for the injury (s 17(1)(b))`
#ASSERT `Can I apply now` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (`a date not used`) 5 TRUE (`d` 1 4 2025) EQUALS `no: after a refusal, or after interim participation ended, only with new medical information or information showing deterioration (s 17(3))`
#ASSERT `Can I apply now` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE (`a date not used`) 5 TRUE (`d` 1 4 2025) EQUALS `an application may be made`
-- s 17(4): a payment received on 10 June 2020, a prescribed 5 years: the period ends 10 June 2025; from 11 June 2025.
#ASSERT `Can I apply now` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 10 6 2020) 5 TRUE (`d` 10 6 2025) EQUALS `not yet: after a s 44(3)(a) payment, an application may be made from` (`d` 11 6 2025)
-- From 11 June 2025 the application may be made, but s 22(4)-(5) lets the agency refuse it without severe hardship.
#ASSERT `Can I apply now` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 10 6 2020) 5 TRUE (`d` 11 6 2025) EQUALS `an application may be made, but after a s 44(3)(a) payment the agency may refuse it even if the injured person is eligible, unless it is satisfied of severe financial hardship (s 22(4)-(5))`
-- A figure under the Act's 5-year floor is raised to 5; 7 years gives 11 June 2027.
#ASSERT `Can I apply now` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 10 6 2020) 3 TRUE (`d` 10 6 2025) EQUALS `not yet: after a s 44(3)(a) payment, an application may be made from` (`d` 11 6 2025)
#ASSERT `Can I apply now` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 10 6 2020) 7 TRUE (`d` 1 1 2027) EQUALS `not yet: after a s 44(3)(a) payment, an application may be made from` (`d` 11 6 2027)
#ASSERT `Can I apply now` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 10 6 2020) 5 FALSE (`d` 1 1 2030) EQUALS `no: after a s 44(3)(a) payment, only in the circumstances prescribed by regulation (s 17(4)(a)(i))`

-- s 18 (with s 10 for "finalised").
#ASSERT `Can this person apply for me` `the injured person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, this person may apply for me`
#ASSERT `Can this person apply for me` `an insurer against whom a claim for the injury has been made` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, the insurer may apply for me, and must give me a copy of the application (s 18(2))`
-- Settled, but the court has not yet sanctioned the settlement: not finalised (s 10(a)), so the insurer may apply.
#ASSERT `Can this person apply for me` `an insurer against whom a claim for the injury has been made` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, the insurer may apply for me, and must give me a copy of the application (s 18(2))`
#ASSERT `Can this person apply for me` `an insurer against whom a claim for the injury has been made` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: an insurer may apply only while its claim for my injury is not finalised (s 18(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can this person apply for me` `an insurer against whom a claim for the injury has been made` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: an insurer may apply only while its claim for my injury is not finalised (s 18(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can this person apply for me` `a parent or guardian of the injured person` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes, this person may apply for me`
-- Fork line 2: a parent of an adult who does not act for them: s 18 does not close its list.
#ASSERT `Can this person apply for me` `a parent or guardian of the injured person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Act does not settle whether this person may apply for me`
#ASSERT `Can this person apply for me` `a parent or guardian of the injured person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes, this person may apply for me`
#ASSERT `Can this person apply for me` `another person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes, this person may apply for me`
#ASSERT `Can this person apply for me` `another person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Act does not settle whether this person may apply for me`

§ `ss 22-23 -- deciding the application`

-- s 22(1)(b): not eligible: refuse, by an information notice (s 23(2)).
#ASSERT `Must the agency accept me into the scheme` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the agency must refuse the application, by an information notice (ss 22(1)(b), 23(2))`
-- s 22(1)(a): Mia is eligible: accept for the participation period.
#ASSERT `Must the agency accept me into the scheme` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the agency must accept the injured person as a participant for the participation period (s 22(1)(a))`
-- s 22(2)-(3): the agency is satisfied her spinal cord injury will keep meeting the criteria: it may accept her for life.
#ASSERT `Must the agency accept me into the scheme` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the agency must accept the injured person as a participant, for the participation period or, if it chooses, for life (s 22(1)(a), (2)-(3))`
-- s 22(4)-(6): eligible, but a s 44(3)(a) payment was received and the agency is not satisfied of severe financial
-- hardship: it may refuse despite s 22(1)(a), or accept on conditions.
#ASSERT `Must the agency accept me into the scheme` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the agency may refuse even though the injured person is eligible; an acceptance may be on conditions, and a refusal or conditions come by an information notice (ss 22(4)-(6), 23(2))`
#ASSERT `Must the agency accept me into the scheme` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the agency may refuse even though the injured person is eligible; an acceptance may be on conditions, and a refusal or conditions come by an information notice (ss 22(4)-(6), 23(2))`
-- The agency is satisfied of severe financial hardship: s 22(4)(b) is not met, so s 22(1)(a) binds.
#ASSERT `Must the agency accept me into the scheme` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the agency must accept the injured person as a participant for the participation period (s 22(1)(a))`
-- Not eligible: the payment changes nothing; refuse.
#ASSERT `Must the agency accept me into the scheme` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the agency must refuse the application, by an information notice (ss 22(1)(b), 23(2))`

§ `schedule 1, ss 21-24, 29, 31-32, 36-39 -- the decision-making period`

-- Mia's application received 2 February 2026, no information request: 28 days later (26 to 28 February, 2 into
-- March) is 2 March 2026. Asked on 2 March: still in time. On 3 March, undecided: taken to be refused (s 24).
#ASSERT `By when must the agency decide` `an application to participate (ss 16, 22)` (`d` 2 2 2026) FALSE (`a date not used`) FALSE (`a date not used`) 0 FALSE (`d` 2 3 2026) EQUALS `the agency must decide by` (`d` 2 3 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must the agency decide` `an application to participate (ss 16, 22)` (`d` 2 2 2026) FALSE (`a date not used`) FALSE (`a date not used`) 0 FALSE (`d` 3 3 2026) EQUALS `taken to be refused (ss 24, 32, 39): the person is entitled to an information notice and may apply for internal review`
#ASSERT `By when must the agency decide` `an application to participate (ss 16, 22)` (`d` 2 2 2026) FALSE (`a date not used`) FALSE (`a date not used`) 0 TRUE (`d` 3 3 2026) EQUALS `the agency has decided`
-- An information request on 20 February (within 28 days), the information given 10 March: 10 March + 28 = 7 April
-- 2026 (21 to 31 March, 7 into April).
#ASSERT `By when must the agency decide` `an application to participate (ss 16, 22)` (`d` 2 2 2026) TRUE (`d` 20 2 2026) TRUE (`d` 10 3 2026) 0 FALSE (`d` 1 4 2026) EQUALS `the agency must decide by` (`d` 7 4 2026)
-- Extended by 14 days (s 22(8)): 21 April 2026. Extended by 40: only 28 allowed: 7 April + 28 = 5 May 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must the agency decide` `an application to participate (ss 16, 22)` (`d` 2 2 2026) TRUE (`d` 20 2 2026) TRUE (`d` 10 3 2026) 14 FALSE (`d` 1 4 2026) EQUALS `the agency must decide by` (`d` 21 4 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must the agency decide` `an application to participate (ss 16, 22)` (`d` 2 2 2026) TRUE (`d` 20 2 2026) TRUE (`d` 10 3 2026) 40 FALSE (`d` 1 4 2026) EQUALS `the agency must decide by` (`d` 5 5 2026)
-- The information not yet given: the period has not started.
#ASSERT `By when must the agency decide` `an application to participate (ss 16, 22)` (`d` 2 2 2026) TRUE (`d` 20 2 2026) FALSE (`a date not used`) 0 FALSE (`d` 1 4 2026) EQUALS `the period has not started: the information the agency asked for has not been given`
-- Fork line 3: an information request on 3 March, after the 28 days of s 21(2) (2 March): not an information request,
-- so the period runs from receipt and ended on 2 March.
#ASSERT `By when must the agency decide` `an application to participate (ss 16, 22)` (`d` 2 2 2026) TRUE (`d` 3 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 10 3 2026) 0 FALSE (`d` 4 3 2026) EQUALS `taken to be refused (ss 24, 32, 39): the person is entitled to an information notice and may apply for internal review`
-- A payment request: no extension power, so the 14 days are ignored: 2 March 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must the agency decide` `a payment request (ss 35, 37)` (`d` 2 2 2026) FALSE (`a date not used`) FALSE (`a date not used`) 14 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `the agency must decide by` (`d` 2 3 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must the agency decide` `a service request (ss 28, 31)` (`d` 2 2 2026) FALSE (`a date not used`) FALSE (`a date not used`) 0 FALSE (`d` 3 3 2026) EQUALS `taken to be refused (ss 24, 32, 39): the person is entitled to an information notice and may apply for internal review`
-- The s 22 rule: 2 February to 2 March is 28 days. Decided on day 28: in time.
#ASSERT `the days from` (`d` 2 2 2026) `to` (`d` 2 3 2026) EQUALS 28
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 22 -- the agency must decide the application within the decision-making period` 28) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the agency` `decide the application` 28)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the agency, "s 24(1): the application was not decided within the decision-making period ..." (day 29)
#TRACE `s 22 -- the agency must decide the application within the decision-making period` 28 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the agency` DOES `decide the application` AT 29

§ `schedule 1, ss 45-48 -- interim participation`

-- Mia, born 10 May 1990, accepted 15 August 2025: 2 years starting that day end on 14 August 2027.
#ASSERT `When does my participation period end` (`d` 10 5 1990) (`d` 15 8 2025) EQUALS `d` 14 8 2027
-- A child born 1 March 2023, accepted 1 September 2025 (aged 2): the period ends when she turns 6, 1 March 2029.
#ASSERT `When does my participation period end` (`d` 1 3 2023) (`d` 1 9 2025) EQUALS `d` 1 3 2029
-- The age-4 edge: born 10 January 2021. Accepted 9 January 2025 (still 3): to the 6th birthday, 10 January 2027.
-- Accepted 10 January 2025 (turned 4 that day): 2 years, to 9 January 2027.
#ASSERT `When does my participation period end` (`d` 10 1 2021) (`d` 9 1 2025) EQUALS `d` 10 1 2027
#ASSERT `When does my participation period end` (`d` 10 1 2021) (`d` 10 1 2025) EQUALS `d` 9 1 2027
-- Born 29 February 2020, accepted at 2: turns 6 in 2026, which has no 29 February: 28 February 2026 (READING).
#ASSERT `When does my participation period end` (`d` 29 2 2020) (`d` 1 6 2022) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2026
-- Accepted 29 February 2024 (an adult): 2 years end the day before 1 March 2026, 28 February 2026.
#ASSERT `When does my participation period end` (`d` 10 5 1990) (`d` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2026
-- s 45(3): a review on 30 June 2027: notice by 2 June 2027 (28 days before). s 47(1): decision 1 July 2027: notice
-- of it by 15 July 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must I be told of a review` (`d` 30 6 2027) EQUALS `d` 2 6 2027
#ASSERT `By when must I be told the review decision` (`d` 1 7 2027) EQUALS `d` 15 7 2027
-- s 46, s 48 for Mia (period ends 14 August 2027).
#ASSERT `What happens at the end of my interim participation` (`d` 10 5 1990) (`d` 15 8 2025) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (`a date not used`) EQUALS `a lifetime participant from the decision (s 46(4))`
#ASSERT `What happens at the end of my interim participation` (`d` 10 5 1990) (`d` 15 8 2025) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (`a date not used`) EQUALS `participation ends at the end of the participation period, on` (`d` 14 8 2027)
#ASSERT `What happens at the end of my interim participation` (`d` 10 5 1990) (`d` 15 8 2025) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 6 2027) EQUALS `participation ends on the earlier day stated in the notice (s 46(5)(b))` (`d` 1 6 2027)
#ASSERT `What happens at the end of my interim participation` (`d` 10 5 1990) (`d` 15 8 2025) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`a date not used`) EQUALS `participation ends at the end of the participation period, on` (`d` 14 8 2027)
-- A stated day after the period ends is not "an earlier day": the end of the period.
#ASSERT `What happens at the end of my interim participation` (`d` 10 5 1990) (`d` 15 8 2025) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 9 2027) EQUALS `participation ends at the end of the participation period, on` (`d` 14 8 2027)
#ASSERT `What happens at the end of my interim participation` (`d` 10 5 1990) (`d` 15 8 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`a date not used`) EQUALS `taken to be no longer eligible: participation ends at the end of the participation period (s 48), on` (`d` 14 8 2027)

§ `ss 9, 35-37 -- paying for care`

-- s 9(1)(c), (2)(a), (3): personal assistance at home from an unregistered carer: excluded. The same in hospital, or
-- from a registered provider: not.
#ASSERT `Is this care excluded` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this care excluded` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is this care excluded` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- s 9(2)(b): care the regulation requires from a registered provider, given by an unregistered one, even in hospital.
#ASSERT `Is this care excluded` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this care excluded` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this care excluded` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this care excluded` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- s 35(3): an expense on 31 August 2026: 6 months later, 31 February does not exist: 28 February 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must I make a payment request` (`d` 31 8 2026) FALSE (`d` 28 2 2027) EQUALS `a payment request may be made, in time, up to` (`d` 28 2 2027)
#ASSERT `By when must I make a payment request` (`d` 31 8 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `late: the agency may accept it only if it considers that fair and reasonable (s 35(4))`
#ASSERT `By when must I make a payment request` (`d` 31 8 2026) TRUE (`d` 1 9 2026) EQUALS `no payment request may be made: the expense falls in the period of my funding agreement (s 35(2))`

-- s 37: $5,000 asked, a prescribed limit of $4,200 (HYPOTHETICAL): an approved service: must approve, pay $4,200.
#ASSERT `Must the agency approve my payment request` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 5000 TRUE 4200 EQUALS `the agency must approve, and pay within 28 days after deciding, in Australian dollars,` 4200
#ASSERT `Must the agency approve my payment request` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 5000 FALSE 0 EQUALS `the agency must approve, and pay within 28 days after deciding, in Australian dollars,` 5000
-- Just under the limit: $4,199 asked: the whole.
#ASSERT `Must the agency approve my payment request` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 4199 TRUE 4200 EQUALS `the agency must approve, and pay within 28 days after deciding, in Australian dollars,` 4199
-- Excluded care in the plan but not specifically stated: not an approved service (s 37(6)): the agency may approve.
#ASSERT `Must the agency approve my payment request` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 5000 TRUE 4200 EQUALS `the agency may approve or refuse (s 37(1), (3)); if it approves it must pay within 28 days after deciding, in Australian dollars, at most` 4200
#ASSERT `Must the agency approve my payment request` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5000 TRUE 4200 EQUALS `the agency must approve, and pay within 28 days after deciding, in Australian dollars,` 4200
-- Incurred during a suspension: taken not to be a participant for division 3 (s 52(6)), so no payment request lies
-- (s 35(1)) (a fork line).
#ASSERT `Must the agency approve my payment request` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 5000 FALSE 0 EQUALS `no payment request lies for an expense incurred during a suspension: the participant is taken not to be a participant for division 3 (ss 35(1), 52(6))`
-- Incurred before acceptance, an approved service now: s 37(2)(a) is not met, so the agency need not approve; it
-- decides under s 37(1); at most the $4,200 limit.
#ASSERT `Must the agency approve my payment request` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 5000 TRUE 4200 EQUALS `the agency need not approve: the expense was not incurred while the person was a participant (s 37(2)(a)); it decides to approve or refuse (s 37(1)); if it approves it must pay within 28 days after deciding, in Australian dollars, at most` 4200
-- s 37(4): approved 15 January 2027: pay by 12 February 2027 (16 to 31 January, 12 into February).
#ASSERT `By when must the agency pay me` (`d` 15 1 2027) EQUALS `d` 12 2 2027
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `s 37 -- the agency must pay an approved payment request within 28 days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the agency` `pay the requested amount` 28)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the agency, "s 37(4): the approved amount was not paid within 28 days after the decision" (day 29)
#TRACE `s 37 -- the agency must pay an approved payment request within 28 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the agency` DOES `pay the requested amount` AT 29

-- s 36: an information request given 1 March 2027 with a due day of 11 March (exactly 10 days later: allowed).
#ASSERT `Has my payment request lapsed` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 11 3 2027) FALSE (`a date not used`) TRUE (`d` 11 3 2027) (`d` 20 3 2027) EQUALS `the payment request has not lapsed`
#ASSERT `Has my payment request lapsed` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 11 3 2027) FALSE (`a date not used`) FALSE (`a date not used`) (`d` 11 3 2027) EQUALS `the payment request lapses unless the information is given by` (`d` 11 3 2027)
#ASSERT `Has my payment request lapsed` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 11 3 2027) FALSE (`a date not used`) FALSE (`a date not used`) (`d` 12 3 2027) EQUALS `the payment request has lapsed (s 36(4))`
-- A later day agreed, 25 March: information given 20 March: not lapsed.
#ASSERT `Has my payment request lapsed` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 11 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 25 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 20 3 2027) (`d` 30 3 2027) EQUALS `the payment request has not lapsed`
-- A due day of 10 March, only 9 days after: earlier than s 36(3) allows (finding 4).
#ASSERT `Has my payment request lapsed` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 10 3 2027) FALSE (`a date not used`) FALSE (`a date not used`) (`d` 20 3 2027) EQUALS `the stated due day is earlier than s 36(3) allows; the Act does not say whether the request can lapse`

